  {
    "sha": "4fbbf7bdec4bd8ea3edca6083c387cc46791c578",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDRmYmJmN2JkZWM0YmQ4ZWEzZWRjYTYwODNjMzg3Y2M0Njc5MWM1Nzg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T05:02:42Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T05:02:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ai): bound the Ollama model selection and name each failure cause\n\nThe automatic selection stopped at the first failed /api/show probe and\nused the 300 s chat time limit for each request. Now a failed probe of\none model does not stop the selection, each request has a 5 s limit and\nthe whole selection has a 20 s limit. Each cause has its own message:\nthe server did not answer its model list, no installed model can call\ntools, the probe failed for a named model, or the time limit ended. A\nchat failure after an automatic selection names the selected model.\n\nThe loopback fixture sets its accepted socket to blocking mode. On\nmacOS the socket inherited the nonblocking mode of the listener and the\nfixture failed at times.\n\nRefs #3782\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "3d8325c130bf860db9909c4d9e9a4aa20e0b2edb",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/3d8325c130bf860db9909c4d9e9a4aa20e0b2edb"
